---
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro"
import Subheading from "../../components/Subheading.astro"

const lastUpdated = "August 2026"
---

<MainLayout
  title="Kompass Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Kompass, an Android compass and level app."
>
  <Subheading title="Kompass Privacy Policy" backLink="/" />

  <section class="my-12">
    <p class="max-w-2xl text-lg">
      Kompass is a compass and level app for Android. This page explains what
      data the app accesses and how it's used.
    </p>
    <p class="max-w-2xl text-sm mt-4 font-light">
      Last updated: {lastUpdated}
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="my-12 max-w-2xl">
    <h3 class="font-medium text-xl text-minion-yellow mb-2">
      The short version
    </h3>
    <p class="mb-4">
      Kompass does not have a server. It never sends any data anywhere. There
      are no accounts, no analytics, no advertising, and no third-party SDKs.
      Everything the app reads from your device is used only to draw the
      compass, level, and related readouts on your own screen, and stays on
      your device.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="my-12 max-w-2xl">
    <h3 class="font-medium text-xl text-minion-yellow mb-2">
      Information the app accesses
    </h3>
    <ul class="leading-8 list-disc list-inside">
      <li>
        <strong>Location</strong> (coarse location, with your permission) — used
        to show your latitude/longitude on screen, to correct the compass for
        true north instead of magnetic north, and to estimate the sun and
        moon's position in the sky. Location is requested only when you use a
        feature that needs it, and is processed entirely on your device.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Motion and environment sensors</strong> (compass/magnetometer,
        accelerometer, barometer) — used to draw the compass heading, the
        bubble level, and the magnetic-field and altitude readouts. This data
        never leaves your device.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your in-app settings</strong> (e.g. haptic feedback on/off,
        default north mode, coordinate display format) — stored locally on
        your device so they persist between app launches. Never transmitted
        anywhere.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="my-12 max-w-2xl">
    <h3 class="font-medium text-xl text-minion-yellow mb-2">
      What Kompass does not do
    </h3>
    <ul class="leading-8 list-disc list-inside">
      <li>It does not collect, transmit, sell, or share any data with anyone, including the developer.</li>
      <li>It does not have user accounts or sign-in.</li>
      <li>It does not use analytics, crash reporting, or advertising SDKs.</li>
      <li>It does not use cookies (it's not a web app).</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="my-12 max-w-2xl">
    <h3 class="font-medium text-xl text-minion-yellow mb-2">
      Children's privacy
    </h3>
    <p>
      Kompass is not directed at children and does not knowingly collect any
      information from children. Since the app has no network access of any
      kind, no information is collected from anyone, of any age.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="my-12 max-w-2xl">
    <h3 class="font-medium text-xl text-minion-yellow mb-2">
      Changes to this policy
    </h3>
    <p>
      If this policy ever changes, the update will be posted on this page
      with a revised "last updated" date above.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="my-12 max-w-2xl">
    <h3 class="font-medium text-xl text-minion-yellow mb-2">Contact</h3>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or the app can be sent to <a
        href="mailto:pavanpej@gmail.com"
        class="text-vivid-blue hover:text-minion-yellow transition-all"
        >pavanpej@gmail.com</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
</MainLayout>
